  "rationale": "FrameInvariants.base_soundness assumes a structurally wellformed class table and an arbitrary counted public trace from initial, concluding WellFormedState, the conjunction of structural and kind correctness. The imported liveness and path-exclusivity statements apply to that result and supply the stated consequences. No claim of progress for untyped programs is made. Rooted-foundation review: the structural invariants now require explicit rootedness (including pending values) plus unique/compatible ownership. Allocation bounds remain solely for freshness; no safety proof assumes edge-age order or global DAG structure. Changed proof selections retain their public statement unless this unit explicitly defines the revised invariant or example. Given/Shared root transport and path reasoning were reviewed by their implementing agents, with fresh review of root-owned unpacking, GC, frame rerooting, class retention and the refill example. Earlier syntax and runtime rules are unchanged. The widened invariant domain is covered by recompilation of all earlier safety proofs and concrete shared-cycle/nonmonotonic-ID regressions, not by a claim that constructors can generate cycles.",
